### 1. Create customer (saves customerId)
POST http://localhost:8081/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Customer",
  "email": "api-test-{{$timestamp}}@example.test",
  "phone": null
}

> {%
  client.test("Customer created", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201"); });
  if (response.status === 201) client.global.set("customerId", String(response.body.id));
%}

### 2. Create empty order (saves orderId)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "deliveryDate": "2026-11-01T12:00:00",
  "shippingAddressId": null,
  "status": "NEW"
}

> {%
  client.test("Order created", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201"); });
  if (response.status === 201) client.global.set("orderId", String(response.body.id));
%}

### 3. List orders (paged; never load all orders at once)
GET http://localhost:8081/orders?page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### 4. Search orders by status
GET http://localhost:8081/orders?status=NEW&page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### 5. Search orders by customer ID
GET http://localhost:8081/orders?customerId={{customerId}}&page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### 6. Search orders by customer and status
GET http://localhost:8081/orders?customerId={{customerId}}&status=NEW&page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### 7. Customer's orders (returns Page<OrdersDTO>, not JPA entities)
GET http://localhost:8081/customers/{{customerId}}/orders?page=0&size=10
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get created order by ID
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Get order lines (empty until orderitems test creates one)
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/items
Accept: application/json

### 10. Update order
PUT http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "deliveryDate": "2026-11-05T14:00:00",
  "shippingAddressId": null,
  "status": "NEW"
}

### 11. Update order status (allowed; cancellation handled separately)
PATCH http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING"
}

### 12. Verify update
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

### 13. Missing order: expected 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/999999999
Accept: application/json

### 14. Cancel: currently expected 409 until stock-safe cancellation is implemented
PATCH http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}

### 15. DELETE empty order only AFTER orderitems test has removed its line
DELETE http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}

### 16. Verify deletion: expected 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json
